 ### [Lanczos Resampling](11246-lanczos-resampling.md)
-Uses a windowed sinc function to balance sharpness with ringing suppression. Chosen when higher fidelity than linear or cubic interpolation is required, particularly in medical imaging.
+Resamples volumetric data by replacing each selected sample with a translated copy of the Lanczos kernel, a limited Sinc function. Distinguishes itself from siblings by using a windowed sinc function that balances sharpness with the suppression of ringing artifacts compared to a pure sinc filter. Chosen when higher fidelity than linear or cubic interpolation is required, particularly in medical imaging contexts where preserving high-frequency details during compression or reconstruction is critical.
 
